DESCRIPTION:<p dir="ltr"><b>Please consider becoming a </b><a href="mailto:
 mscg-compost-updates@googlegroups.com"><b><u>volunteer</u></b></a><b> or ma
 king a </b><a href="https://maplestreetcommunitygarden.org/donate"><b><u>do
 nation </u></b></a><b>to support our local\, community project run entirely
  by volunteers. </b></p><p dir="ltr"><b>We post unexpected closures on </b>
 <a href="https://www.instagram.com/maplestreetgarden/"><b><u>Instagram</u><
 /b></a><b>. </b></p><p dir="ltr">*We ask that you follow the below protocol
  and best practices: </p><p dir="ltr"><b>PLEASE CHOP ALL YOUR SCRAPS </b>(c
 ut up anything big\, like whole squash/melon or citrus)<b> and TAKE OFF all
  stickers and rubber bands. </b></p><p dir="ltr"><b>WE ACCEPT ONLY:</b></p>
 <ul><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Fruit &amp\; vegetable scraps</p></li><li di
 r="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Coffee grounds &amp\; filters (brown filters preferred
 !)</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Tea bags (non-metal\, only paper)</p>
 </li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Egg and Nut shells</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p
  dir="ltr">Clean + dry leaves (no street leaves please)</p></li><li dir="lt
 r"><p dir="ltr">Paper Towls (brown preferred)</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir=
 "ltr">Paper plates and bowls</p></li></ul><br><p dir="ltr"><b>DO NOT BRING:
  </b></p><ul><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Rice\, pasta\, bread\, cereal\, or 
 grains</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Meat\, Chicken or Fish </p></li><
 li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Fats or Oils</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">D
 airy products or byproducts</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Animal Waste
  or Hair </p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Litter or bedding</p></li><li 
 dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Dried or cut flowers (conventional flowers typically
  carry a<a href="https://www.nwf.org/en/Magazines/National-Wildlife/2000/Pe
 sticides-and-Cut-Flowers"><u> </u><u>LOT of pesticides</u></a>\, please lim
 it them in our compost)</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">House plants &am
 p\; potting soil *please <u>do not compost plants that are diseased</u> or 
 infested with bugs</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Ornamental items like
  wreaths &amp\; Christmas trees- <u>sticks and twigs do not break down</u> 
 in our compost\, please either chop them into very small pieces or leave th
 em curbside</p></li></ul><br><b>To sign up on our Compost Updates list so y
 ou can receive email notifications when we unexpectedly close (due to weath
 er or low volunteer turnout)\, when we reopen in spring or close for the wi
 nter\, sign up </b><a href="mailto:mscg-compost-updates@googlegroups.com"><
 b><u>here</u></b></a><b>. </b>
